\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Ten-taxon scaling diagnostic.} The older four-method probability--reward view shows the collapse signature for GRPO and count IPS and broad sampled support for the multiplicity-aware methods. Because methods sample different terminal sets, this is a within-policy diagnostic rather than a shared-outcome benchmark.}}{12}{figure.appendix.4}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Ten-taxon matched-transform view.} Linear and log--log transforms are shown consistently across methods. Interpret each correlation as a property of that policy's self-sampled support; a fixed-tree comparison on identical outcomes remains pending.}}{13}{figure.appendix.5}\protected@file@percent }
